  "question": {
    "text": "The calculated spin-only magnetic moments of $\\mathrm{K}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_6\\right]$ and $\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_6\\right]$ respectively are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bKkhG",
      "text": "3.87 and 4.90 B.M.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FwZ54",
      "text": "4.90 and 5.92 B.M.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "keiAG",
      "text": "4.90 and 4.90 B.M.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gjfxY",
      "text": "5.92 and 4.90 B.M.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{K}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_6\\right] \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+} \\Rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+} \\text { with } \\mathrm{OH}^{-}(\\mathrm{WFL}) \\\\\n& =\\mathrm{t}_{29}{ }^3 \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}{ }^2\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nNumber of unpaired electron ( $n$ ) $=5$\n$\\mu$ spin only $=5.92 \\mathrm{BM}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_6\\right] \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\mathrm{(WFL)} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \\Rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^6=\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^4 \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{n}=4\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\mu_{\\text {spin only }}=4.90 \\mathrm{BM}$",
    "image": null
  },
